"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkp_vs_np_docs=globalThis.webpackChunkp_vs_np_docs||[]).push([[1975],{2490(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"tag":{"label":"lower-bounds","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/tags/lower-bounds","allTagsPath":"/azeon/p-vs-np/tags","count":6,"items":[{"id":"failed-proofs/circuit-complexity-primer","title":"Circuit Complexity Primer","description":"Forget programs and tapes. A Boolean circuit is computation drawn as a diagram of AND, OR and NOT gates. Most functions need gigantic circuits, yet we can\'t prove it for a single function we care about.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/failed-proofs/circuit-complexity-primer"},{"id":"failed-proofs/the-burden-of-proof","title":"The Burden of Proof","description":"To prove P = NP, you need one algorithm. To prove P \u2260 NP, you need to rule out every algorithm that could ever exist. And a strange twist: if P = NP, an algorithm that works is already written down.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/failed-proofs/the-burden-of-proof"},{"id":"failed-proofs/the-challenges-of-gct","title":"The Challenges of GCT","description":"Geometric Complexity Theory hoped the simplest kind of obstruction would be enough. In 2016, three mathematicians proved it can\'t be. Here\'s what that setback means, and what\'s still alive.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/failed-proofs/the-challenges-of-gct"},{"id":"real-world-impact/the-cost-of-inefficiency","title":"The Cost of Inefficiency","description":"How much money does the world lose because we can\'t solve NP-Hard problems perfectly? I went looking for the number. Nobody can honestly calculate it, and the reason is itself a lesson about NP-Hardness.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/the-cost-of-inefficiency"},{"id":"failed-proofs/the-natural-proofs-barrier","title":"The Natural Proofs Barrier","description":"Razborov and Rudich noticed that every circuit lower bound proof of their time had the same simple shape. Then they proved that, if strong cryptography exists, no proof of that shape can ever separate P from NP.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/failed-proofs/the-natural-proofs-barrier"},{"id":"failed-proofs/why-havent-we-solved-it","title":"Why Haven\'t We Solved It?","description":"Over fifty years, thousands of researchers, and almost no progress on the main question. It\'s not lack of effort. It\'s that mathematicians have proved, three separate times, that whole families of proof techniques cannot work.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/failed-proofs/why-havent-we-solved-it"}],"unlisted":false}}')}}]);